-- ===========================================================================
-- tests-simplex-draft.l4 — the SimpLEX test table, transcribed, run against
-- THE DRAFT, in the table's own outcome words. Expected values are the
-- table's, copied from the screenshot; none was taken from the code.
--
-- Every row's outcome column, and every row's reference column, is asserted.
-- Row 8's outcome rests on the draft's regulation 4, which the screenshot
-- does not show; it is read from the panel's own gloss of it (fork F2).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `The SimpLEX table against the draft`

§§ `Row 5 — הרשמה לבחינה עיונית → הרשמה מאושרת, תקנה 2(א)`

#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `registration approved` `holds for` `row 5 — registration for a theoretical exam` `under` `the draft`
#ASSERT `the sub-regulation that sets the fee for` (`taking` `a theoretical exam`) `under` `the draft` EQUALS JUST "2(א)"

§§ `Row 6 — הרשמה לבחינה מעשית → הרשמה מאושרת, תקנה 2(ב)`

#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `registration approved` `holds for` `row 6 — registration for a practical exam` `under` `the draft`
#ASSERT `the sub-regulation that sets the fee for` (`taking` `a practical exam`) `under` `the draft` EQUALS JUST "2(ב)"

§§ `Row 7 — ערעור עם תשלום (₪ 40) → הערעור נבדק, תקנה 2(ג)`

#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `the appeal is examined` `holds for` `row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a theoretical exam` `under` `the draft`
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `the appeal is examined` `holds for` `row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a practical exam` `under` `the draft`
#ASSERT `the sub-regulation that sets the fee for` (`an objection to the grade of` `a theoretical exam`) `under` `the draft` EQUALS JUST "2(ג)"
#ASSERT `the sub-regulation that sets the fee for` (`an objection to the grade of` `a practical exam`) `under` `the draft` EQUALS JUST "2(ג)"
-- "(₪ 40)": the amount the row pays is the draft's fee.
#ASSERT `the fee for` (`an objection to the grade of` `a theoretical exam`) `under` `the draft` EQUALS JUST 40

§§ `Row 8 — הרשמה לבחינה ללא תשלום → השעיית שירות, תקנה 4`

#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `suspension of service` `holds for` `row 8 — registration for a theoretical exam without payment` `under` `the draft`
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `suspension of service` `holds for` `row 8 — registration for a practical exam without payment` `under` `the draft`

§§ `The worked example — מועמד נרשם לבחינה עיונית אבל לא משלם את האגרה → הרשמה נדחית – חובה להשלים תשלום`

#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `registration rejected — payment must be completed` `holds for` `the worked example — a candidate registers for a theoretical exam but does not pay the fee` `under` `the draft`

-- The example's first ground, "סעיף 9(א): מחייב מעבר בחינה", is tested against
-- the Law in tests-law.l4: s. 9(a) of the Law as enacted says nothing about
-- an exam; the exam requirement is in s. 2's definition of "תעודת גמר".
